  "status_text": "When can one flip reach the gate lower bound? On selections that touch every line, a circuit must report whether each marked line has exactly one selected end. For at least three distinct marked endpoints and at most one NOT, Lean checked a lower bound of one gate per marked endpoint plus one per marked line. It can be met exactly when every two marked endpoints are joined and the sets left after removing each marked line's ends from the marked endpoints are pairwise nested or disjoint. Constants are free and gates read at most two earlier wires (L-lib-1190).",
